# Grammar and spelling

Correct grammar and consistent spelling improve clarity and reduce reader friction.

## Core rules

- Use present tense for descriptions of the current product state
- Prefer active voice
- Use second person by default
- Avoid ambiguous pronouns
- Avoid gendered pronouns when possible
- Use contractions appropriately
- Keep sentence structure straightforward

## American English

Use American English unless the product or UI explicitly uses another spelling.

Examples:
- organize, not organise
- color, not colour
- behavior, not behaviour
- analyze, not analyse

## Punctuation

- Use the Oxford comma in lists of three or more items
- Use commas after introductory phrases
- Keep punctuation inside closing quotation marks in standard U.S. usage
- Use a colon to introduce a list or explanation

## Abbreviations

- Spell out the full name on first use when needed
- Use abbreviations consistently thereafter
- Avoid Latin abbreviations such as e.g. and i.e.
- Prefer "for example" and "such as"

## A few examples

### Good
- If you don't select all required permissions, an error message appears.
- Use the `cluster_admin` role for administrative actions.
- The feature works with the default settings.

### Avoid
- If you didn't select all the required permissions, an error message will appear.
- Use the "cluster_admin" role.
- The feature is able to be configured.

## Capitalization

- Capitalize the first word of a sentence
- Capitalize product names and proper nouns
- Use sentence-style capitalization for headings and labels
- Do not capitalize common nouns unless required by UI or title conventions
